% Persistent-consequent menu exclusion fixture (TODO_0277 audit).
% The trigger rule PRODUCES a persistent menu at t=5 whose alternative
% carries a before-window (D15 bars stamped costs under !, windows are
% embedded-antecedent-legal) — the coalescer must treat wood as
% stamp-load-bearing from the start (durable exclusion via the consequent
% walk over alt.persistent), even though no menu exists in the state yet.
% iron is observed by nothing.
wood: type.
plank: type.
iron: type.
dummy: type.
trigger: type.

mk: trigger -o { !( (wood * before 100 -o { plank })
                  & (dummy -o { plank }) ) }@5.

% trigger@4: the producer is PENDING at the settle-3 coalesce point — the
% menu does not exist yet, so only the durable consequent walk excludes wood.
#expect_menu_producer (settle: 3)
  trigger@4 * wood@2 * wood@3 * iron@1
  =>
  !_2 wood .
